{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0121YwMjwRMw15Uoh32ooVPY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# WI-275 — Windows shim-refusal-aware fixtures for the two SR-026 launch tests\n2\t\n3\t**WI:** WI-275 · **Status:** queued · **Delivers:** SR-026 (test layer only —\n4\tno product change)\n5\t\n6\t## Problem\n7\t\n8\tTwo tests are red on Windows at HEAD — verified 2026-07-23 on the dev box\n9\t(3.11.9 venv, pinned toolchain; full suite otherwise green: 1369 passed /\n10\t5 skipped / 2 failed) and verified **pre-existing** (identical failures on a\n11\tclean tree before the day's dial/filing commits). Both are green on\n12\tmacOS/POSIX, which is why the owner's macOS runs never saw them:\n13\t\n14\t1. `tests/test_agent_loop.py::test_cmd_shim_cli_spawns_on_windows` — the WI-120\n15\t   regression test (a `.cmd`-shim CLI must spawn via the which-resolved path).\n16\t2. `tests/test_session_stdin.py::test_run_session_codex_reads_last_message_not_transcript`\n17\t   — the WI-217 codex `--output-last-message` capture test (Windows arm builds\n18\t   a `codextest.cmd` shim).\n19\t\n20\tRoot cause is not the product: the H-4 BatBadBut hardening (repo-review\n21\t2026-07-21, remediated in `272a6e8`) added\n22\t`agent_session._validate_prompt_transport`, which **refuses prompt-in-argv\n23\tlaunches through a Windows batch shim** — `_batch_prompt_error` fires whenever\n24\t`stdin_input is None` and `argv[0]` resolves (directly or via `shutil.which`)\n25\tto `.cmd`/`.bat`. That refusal is deliberate, tested behavior. The two fixtures\n26\tpredate it and collide with it:\n27\t\n28\t- Test 1's `--agent-cmd` fixture template carries `-p {prompt}` — prompt-in-argv\n29\t  — so the launch it asserts must succeed is now (correctly) refused.\n30\t- Test 2 calls `al.run_session([str(launcher)], tmp_path, 30)` with no stdin\n31\t  delivery, so the guard fires on the bare `.cmd` launcher even though no\n32\t  prompt token is present — while the *real* codex rows deliver the prompt via\n33\t  stdin (`stdin_input is not None`, WI-216/217) and never trip it.\n34\t\n35\t**Why this fronts the queue (Priority 1, the column's first use):** the branch\n36\tis unpushed, so CI — which runs the suite on Windows (3.11 + latest) — has\n37\tnever seen these reds; on push the Windows legs go red, blocking the\n38\t`dualplan-routing-fix` merge path. Everything else about the fix is small.\n39\t\n40\t## Approach\n41\t\n42\tTest-layer only; the H-4 guard, `build_argv`, and `run_session` are untouched.\n43\tMake each fixture exercise its *original* concern through the transport the\n44\tproduct now prescribes:\n45\t\n46\t- **Test 1 (WI-120 spawn):** drop `-p {prompt}` from the fixture's\n47\t  `--agent-cmd` template so the prompt rides stdin (the WI-216 path), and make\n48\t  the fake CLI read the prompt from stdin where its assertions need it. The\n49\t  `.cmd` shim still spawns through the which-resolved path — WI-120's\n50\t  CreateProcess concern stays fully tested — and the launch is now\n51\t  transport-legal. Optionally add the cheap negative arm: the *same* shim with\n52\t  a `{prompt}` template is refused with the H-4 message (locks both invariants\n53\t  in one place).\n54\t- **Test 2 (WI-217 capture):** call `run_session` the way the coordinator\n55\t  actually launches codex — with stdin prompt delivery (`stdin_input` not\n56\t  None), matching the real no-`{prompt}` codex CmdTemplate. The `.cmd` launcher\n57\t  then passes the guard and the `--output-last-message` capture assertion runs\n58\t  as designed. (Alternative if the signature makes that awkward: a native-exe\n59\t  launcher — e.g. a copied `sys.executable` named `codextest.exe` — but stdin\n60\t  delivery is truer to the seam under test; prefer it.)\n61\t- **POSIX arms unchanged** — both tests already pass there; the edits must not\n62\t  alter the non-Windows fixtures' behavior.\n63\t- Guard against silent weakening: neither fix may delete the WI-120/WI-217\n64\t  assertions or skip the tests on Windows — the point is that both invariants\n65\t  (spawn resolution, capture) hold *under the hardened transport rule*.\n66\t\n67\t## Interfaces\n68\t\n69\tNo cross-module seam — acts only within `tests/test_agent_loop.py` and\n70\t`tests/test_session_stdin.py` (intra-module, test layer). Nearest seam for\n71\treference: the\n72\t`build_argv`/`run_session` prompt-transport contract in\n73\t`project-trajectory/scripts/agent_session.py` (LLR-026, SR-026), unchanged.\n74\t\n75\t## Done-when\n76\t\n77\t- [ ] Both tests pass on Windows against the H-4 guard (the 2026-07-23 repro\n78\t      box goes 1371+ passed / 0 failed apart from environmental skips).\n79\t- [ ] Both tests still pass on POSIX (CI Linux/macOS legs stay green).\n80\t- [ ] The WI-120 spawn assertion and the WI-217 capture assertion survive\n81\t      verbatim in intent (no skip/delete on Windows).\n82\t- [ ] Commit bar green (`pytest -q -n auto -m smoke` + `check_docs.py`).\n83\t- [ ] Row set `done` (Deliverable filled, SpecRef cleared); spec archived to\n84\t      `docs/archive/specs/` with close date.\n85\t\n86\t## Notes / open questions\n87\t\n88\t- Filed 2026-07-23 (owner directive) as its own quick WI rather than a WI-274\n89\t  part C: different concern (test fixtures vs dev-environment ergonomics),\n90\t  different files, and it gates the merge path where WI-274 does not.\n91\t- If the build session finds test 2's `run_session` call cannot carry\n92\t  `stdin_input` without touching product code, stop and re-scope — the\n93\t  test-layer-only boundary is the spec's hard edge.\n94\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"918e6987-c369-4ba8-80a8-34edb5f9d4fd","uuid":"22482cdd-e917-49eb-b376-b03bc9d51d28","timestamp":"2026-07-23T07:14:51.628Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template-trains\\1-g3-WI-275-dfea\\docs\\specs\\WI-275.md","content":"# WI-275 — Windows shim-refusal-aware fixtures for the two SR-026 launch tests\n\n**WI:** WI-275 · **Status:** queued · **Delivers:** SR-026 (test layer only —\nno product change)\n\n## Problem\n\nTwo tests are red on Windows at HEAD — verified 2026-07-23 on the dev box\n(3.11.9 venv, pinned toolchain; full suite otherwise green: 1369 passed /\n5 skipped / 2 failed) and verified **pre-existing** (identical failures on a\nclean tree before the day's dial/filing commits). Both are green on\nmacOS/POSIX, which is why the owner's macOS runs never saw them:\n\n1. `tests/test_agent_loop.py::test_cmd_shim_cli_spawns_on_windows` — the WI-120\n   regression test (a `.cmd`-shim CLI must spawn via the which-resolved path).\n2. `tests/test_session_stdin.py::test_run_session_codex_reads_last_message_not_transcript`\n   — the WI-217 codex `--output-last-message` capture test (Windows arm builds\n   a `codextest.cmd` shim).\n\nRoot cause is not the product: the H-4 BatBadBut hardening (repo-review\n2026-07-21, remediated in `272a6e8`) added\n`agent_session._validate_prompt_transport`, which **refuses prompt-in-argv\nlaunches through a Windows batch shim** — `_batch_prompt_error` fires whenever\n`stdin_input is None` and `argv[0]` resolves (directly or via `shutil.which`)\nto `.cmd`/`.bat`. That refusal is deliberate, tested behavior. The two fixtures\npredate it and collide with it:\n\n- Test 1's `--agent-cmd` fixture template carries `-p {prompt}` — prompt-in-argv\n  — so the launch it asserts must succeed is now (correctly) refused.\n- Test 2 calls `al.run_session([str(launcher)], tmp_path, 30)` with no stdin\n  delivery, so the guard fires on the bare `.cmd` launcher even though no\n  prompt token is present — while the *real* codex rows deliver the prompt via\n  stdin (`stdin_input is not None`, WI-216/217) and never trip it.\n\n**Why this fronts the queue (Priority 1, the column's first use):** the branch\nis unpushed, so CI — which runs the suite on Windows (3.11 + latest) — has\nnever seen these reds; on push the Windows legs go red, blocking the\n`dualplan-routing-fix` merge path. Everything else about the fix is small.\n\n## Approach\n\nTest-layer only; the H-4 guard, `build_argv`, and `run_session` are untouched.\nMake each fixture exercise its *original* concern through the transport the\nproduct now prescribes:\n\n- **Test 1 (WI-120 spawn):** drop `-p {prompt}` from the fixture's\n  `--agent-cmd` template so the prompt rides stdin (the WI-216 path), and make\n  the fake CLI read the prompt from stdin where its assertions need it. The\n  `.cmd` shim still spawns through the which-resolved path — WI-120's\n  CreateProcess concern stays fully tested — and the launch is now\n  transport-legal. Optionally add the cheap negative arm: the *same* shim with\n  a `{prompt}` template is refused with the H-4 message (locks both invariants\n  in one place).\n- **Test 2 (WI-217 capture):** call `run_session` the way the coordinator\n  actually launches codex — with stdin prompt delivery (`stdin_input` not\n  None), matching the real no-`{prompt}` codex CmdTemplate. The `.cmd` launcher\n  then passes the guard and the `--output-last-message` capture assertion runs\n  as designed. (Alternative if the signature makes that awkward: a native-exe\n  launcher — e.g. a copied `sys.executable` named `codextest.exe` — but stdin\n  delivery is truer to the seam under test; prefer it.)\n- **POSIX arms unchanged** — both tests already pass there; the edits must not\n  alter the non-Windows fixtures' behavior.\n- Guard against silent weakening: neither fix may delete the WI-120/WI-217\n  assertions or skip the tests on Windows — the point is that both invariants\n  (spawn resolution, capture) hold *under the hardened transport rule*.\n\n## Interfaces\n\nNo cross-module seam — acts only within `tests/test_agent_loop.py` and\n`tests/test_session_stdin.py` (intra-module, test layer). Nearest seam for\nreference: the\n`build_argv`/`run_session` prompt-transport contract in\n`project-trajectory/scripts/agent_session.py` (LLR-026, SR-026), unchanged.\n\n## Done-when\n\n- [ ] Both tests pass on Windows against the H-4 guard (the 2026-07-23 repro\n      box goes 1371+ passed / 0 failed apart from environmental skips).\n- [ ] Both tests still pass on POSIX (CI Linux/macOS legs stay green).\n- [ ] The WI-120 spawn assertion and the WI-217 capture assertion survive\n      verbatim in intent (no skip/delete on Windows).\n- [ ] Commit bar green (`pytest -q -n auto -m smoke` + `check_docs.py`).\n- [ ] Row set `done` (Deliverable filled, SpecRef cleared); spec archived to\n      `docs/archive/specs/` with close date.\n\n## Notes / open questions\n\n- Filed 2026-07-23 (owner directive) as its own quick WI rather than a WI-274\n  part C: different concern (test fixtures vs dev-environment ergonomics),\n  different files, and it gates the merge path where WI-274 does not.\n- If the build session finds test 2's `run_session` call cannot carry\n  `stdin_input` without touching product code, stop and re-scope — the\n  test-layer-only boundary is the spec's hard edge.\n","numLines":94,"startLine":1,"totalLines":94}}}
